WEBVTT

00:34:58.520 --> 00:35:00.988
then you actually do get to find

00:35:01.012 --> 00:35:04.176
who's actually elevating the performance
of the people around them.

00:35:04.200 --> 00:35:06.436
And I find that to be so difficult to see

00:35:06.460 --> 00:35:08.176
in a traditional interview process.

00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:09.684
Is that by design?

00:35:09.708 --> 00:35:13.917
RS: Absolutely, you know,
but what we're not focused on,

00:35:13.941 --> 00:35:16.028
which kind of blows
a lot of people's minds,

00:35:16.052 --> 00:35:18.289
is individual performance.

00:35:18.313 --> 00:35:20.513
We want the performance of the team.

00:35:20.983 --> 00:35:23.881
AG: This is what I'd love
to see more workplaces do.

00:35:23.905 --> 00:35:26.913
Yeah, coding skills
are important to be a programmer,

00:35:26.937 --> 00:35:30.022
but it's often easier
to teach skills than values.